  "notes": [
    "KPA-48, measured: passing acc_path alone (which is what contour.py:1390 does) takes 0.008 s and returns an accumulation field that is the same as the raster supplied (max difference 0.0 cells; supplied max 67199, recomputed max 67199). Passing both paths takes 0.034 s and does read the supplied raster (True). The baseline accumulation is crest-split and the recompute is not, so the keyline runs on a pond-uncorrected field.",
    "SWL-22, measured: suggest_spacing omits infiltration_mm_hr, so the capacity it hands capture_spacing is short by up to 85.7% (Sand / 24 h). A lower capacity gives a TIGHTER advised interval, so the direction is O (over-sizes), not U.",
    "CTL-01, measured: suggest_spacing calls slope_statistics with no mask (contour.py:168) though the parameter exists and is unit-tested. On this fixture the site-wide median slope is 8.06 deg and the middle-half median is 6.81 deg, a change of -15.5%. The docstring at contour.py:137 says the advice is read 'over the usable area'; it is read site-wide.",
    "MHL-01, measured: haul_regions over block_m 0.01 -> 1000 m (a 100,000x range) produces 1 distinct output(s). `block` is computed at mass_haul.py:124 and passed to _regions_from, which never reads it. earthworks.py, the only caller, never passes block_m at all, so the parameter is inert in two independent ways.",
    "IMP-02, measured: transect_cells searches +/-200 m and returns a crest line spanning 400 m, while the refusal compares the TOTAL run against 200 m. Code and message agree with each other; the docstring's 'either side' describes a limit twice as permissive as the one enforced.",
    "knob sweep not run (pass --sweep; it is ~20 harness runs)"
  ],
